# SHA-256 of every upstream file this package ships unmodified from BLAKE3
# 1.8.7 (tag 1.8.7, commit f3149ec5bb5449af877ba20377a11008ff499fa2,
# https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3).
#
# 52 records, and the set is exactly the upstream-owned entries of build.zig.zon
# `.paths`: the whole c/ directory, the known-answer fixture
# test_vectors/test_vectors.json, the three licence texts, and upstream's
# README preserved as README.upstream.md. It is a subset of the upstream tree,
# not a copy of it. The Rust
# crate (src/, b3sum/, build.rs, benches/, reference_impl/, tools/, media/) is
# carried in this repository for provenance, is not referenced by anything in
# the package, and is deliberately not listed here.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason:
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, zig/, runtime/, tests.zig, smoke.zig, consumer/,
#   package.nix, flake.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml, .envrc and
#   .github/workflows/verify.yml -- this fork's own files, listed in NOTICE.md.
#   README.md -- this fork's own README, written by this fork; upstream's README
#   is the identical upstream file under the name README.upstream.md, and its
#   digest is the one recorded below. The relocation moved the path, not a byte.
#   .gitignore -- upstream's two lines are kept verbatim and this fork appends
#   its own Zig entries, so the file is not byte-identical to upstream.
#   UPSTREAM.sha256 itself -- a record cannot contain its own digest.
#
# These are the bytes in this working tree, hashed as a raw byte read (Bun
# File.arrayBuffer, SHA-256 from node:crypto) on 2026-10-01. They are not a
# signature and not a Git object id: see UPSTREAM.md, "Integrity", for what
# they do and do not establish.
#
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
